{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/513954-what-was-melinda-from-hunter-s-blues","id":513954,"title":"What was Melinda, from \"Hunter's Blues\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-14T01:18:23-07:00","id":513954,"title":"What was Melinda, from \"Hunter's Blues\"?","content":"Does anyone know what sort of being Melinda (from Scott Ciencin's 'Hunter's Blues&quot;) was? She's clearly not human - she's immune to the Delirium, for one thing, and has ruby red eyes (obvious even to mundanes), just for starters.<br /> <br /> However, I don't recognize what she actually <i>is</i>. She describes herself as having been, &quot;Snow White, but I drifted&quot; . . . without going into any further details. &quot;Others of her kind&quot; had to steal her body before an autopsy, but (in life) she doesn't seem to demonstrate any obvious abilities (certainly not regeneration). Except for <i>maybe</i> some sort of sex aura . . . The story repeatedly describes her as beautiful and incredibly desirable - and offended if guys <i>aren't</i> instantly attracted to her.<br /> <br /> So . . . any ideas? She's not fomori/bakemono, has no problem working with the Garou, and predates the release of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>. And she's mortal enough to die from a gunshot wound. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-14-2015, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:37:25-07:00","id":514061,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the 'red 'eyes' appeared in a bunch of stories, but was never expanded on. (They could also see through Obfuscate type powers.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T00:25:02-07:00","id":539332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/513954-what-was-melinda-from-hunter-s-blues?p=514061#post514061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the 'red 'eyes' appeared in a bunch of stories, but was never expanded on. (They could also see through Obfuscate type powers.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Do you remember any of the others? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T09:34:01-07:00","id":539650,"title":"","content":"I know there was a book of short stories, the only thing I can remember offhand is Sam Haight scoping out something and one of the 'red eyes' out with some trick or treaters waving at him through whatever stealth power he was using.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T20:35:38-07:00","id":540450,"title":"","content":"Certainly fits within the abilities of a DA:Fae Changeling though that was unlikely the intention of the authors..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T03:23:02-07:00","id":1263522,"title":"","content":"In the end of the story, Donovan thought she was fallen angel but &quot;Hunter's Blues&quot; predates the release of Demon the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12954-adrax","name":"Adrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T09:49:51-07:00","id":1263603,"title":"","content":"Back in the day, the sixth anthology collection of White Wolf/World of Darkness short fiction was 1995's <b>City of Darkness: Unseen</b>, and several of those stories had appearances by the people with red eyes. A few of them also appeared in the other anthologies (the original 1990s versions): <i>Death and Damnation</i> for Wraith, <i>Truth Until Paradox</i> for Mage, and <i>The Splendor Falls</i> for Changeling. I really can't recall if <i>The Beast Within</i> for Vampire had any red eye stories or not. Likewise for the Harper-Collins novels which were published around the same time period. <br /> <br /> The red eyed people were clearly supposed to &quot;mean something&quot;, but exactly what was never explained. I once asked Wraith Developer Richard Dansky about it, but even he didn't know what they were supposed to be. It appears to be something the Fiction Department (under Stewart Wieck IIRC) had come up with. The two most common theories I've heard is that it was either some sort of Changeling metaplot point that was dropped during the development of the first edition (most of these anthology stories were set in San Fransisco, which was supposed to be Changeling's signature city) or that it was the original idea that eventually grew into both Hunter: The Reckoning and the Red Star that appeared before the Time of Judgment. The actual truth is anyone's guess. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T15:19:27-08:00","id":1264647,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Changeling, either related to Balor or maybe referring to the heroes/mortals of the Fairytales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}